<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ausetani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.) · capital Ausa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Iberian people of the plain of Vic in Catalonia, whose name survives in the later County of Osona.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ausetani lived on the plain of Vic and the surrounding hills in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a> from about the 5th century BCE. Their chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vic">Ausa</a>, on the site of modern Vic, and the fortified settlement of L'Esquerda lay nearby.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their institutions beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy's</a> narrative. They lived from farming and herding, and minted coins with the Iberian legend Ausesken. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> they sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, and their leader Amusicus fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-barca">Hasdrubal</a> when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> besieged their town for thirty days.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After further resistance during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato</a>'s campaign of 195 BCE, they were absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vic">Ausa</a> became the Roman town of Ausa, later Vicus Ausonensis, and their name lived on in the medieval <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-osona">County of Osona</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ausetani.jpg" alt="Ausetani" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: rgonzalez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ausesken_1b_dels_Ausetans.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ausa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Amusicus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ausetans</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=ausetani" aria-label="Ausetani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4735 685 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ausetani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5055 941L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5055 941h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5055 941h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ausa. <a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=ausetani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
